Z||000000||LZeitgeist||09-09-2001||06:20 PM||||On Saturday, Sept. 15th, Crown Pontiac in Greensboro is sponsoring a Cruise Night from 6pm to 9pm. (That means have your car ready to roll out at 6:00pm.)<P>These are the directions I was given to get there from Raleigh...<P>Going down 40 West/85 South, when 40 and 85 split, stay on 40 (like you are heading towards Winston-Salem). Take the exit *AFTER* the one you would normally take to go to Four Seasons Mall (visible on the left side of the highway). The dealership is (supposedly) visible from this exit, so turn accordingly. <P>If you see a muscular-looking guy there with a white/blue 25th Anniversary Ram Air Trans Am, tell him that the guy from Raleigh with the red Fiero Formula sent you... I don't think I'll be able to go (when I last talked to him, I told him I'd see him there, but then I remembered a prior commitment I'd made some time ago...)<P>Have fun... <BR><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||09-09-2001||07:00 PM||||Sounds like a plan to me.  Let's get some Fieros down there!!!<P>You coming Galen?  Oh, sorry - it's too far to walk.  I forgot.||||reg||1
